i-74.1","metadata":{"agent_clan":"bob-cli-74","agent_clan_generation":"20261012234040","bead_id":"bob-cli-74.1","changespec_name":"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli","cl_name":"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli","clan_summary":"[bold #D75FFF]◆ EPIC bob-cli-74[/bold #D75FFF]\n[dim]  Title: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]Pull an emptied project's ^prj in as a successor link, on the ^prj [/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]         [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]line model[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]When a close gesture completes the last remaining task of a project[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]note, its ^prj task is linked right after the closed task's link, [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]becomes Next, and loses its hide tag in the same write. This works [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]in bob capture (! and =x) and in Obsidian (Ctrl+Enter, Alt+]). [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]\"Empty\" is exactly bob projects sync's surface predicate, so sync [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]never re-hides a pulled-in ^prj. docs/task-dependencies.md [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]§12.10/§12.11 become true (resolving bob-cli-6x). bob-cli just [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]check fails only the bob-cli-6m tests, and bob-plugins npm test [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]fails only the known bob-cli-6v, bob-cli-6w and bob-cli-3w cases. [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]The new bob and plugins are installed on this host and, when [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]reachable, on the MacBook.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]6[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]4[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202610/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]project_pull_in_line_model.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202610/project_pull_in_line_model.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]bob-cli-74[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/bobs-org/bob-cli--beads/blob/main/pages/bob-cli-74/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Reconcile the §12.10 pull-in contract with sync and the [/bold #D7AFFF]      [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]shipped line model[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]contract[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]contract: make §12.10 EMPTY exactly bob projects sync's surface [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]predicate (dated recount, plannable recognition, marker-line sub-project[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]states, sync's schedule), specify the recover-rank \\[unblocked::] [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]ordering, the PROJECT RECOVERY cascade, surfaced rows, SL20 and the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]still-blocked reason shape, fix the freshness §5 cross-refs, and add [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]PP25–PP28.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Shared sync surface predicate and the Rust pull-in planner[/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]cli-model[dim] · [dim][/dim]after contract[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]cli-model: factor sync's surface predicate into one crate-visible [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]projects helper, widen normalize_task_hide_tag, add the pure [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]task_complete/project_pull_in.rs planner, wire it into plan_successors [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF](gate, merge, breaker, #hide edit, \\[unblocked::], cascade, row fields), [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and pin the planner-level PP vectors.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Project pull-in in bob capture ! and =x closes, JSON and human[bold black on #FFD75F][/bold #D7AFFF] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]output[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]cli-capture[dim] · [dim][/dim]after cli-model[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]cli-capture: keep id-less C in the ! and =x close paths, feed staged [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]project-note text to the planner, build the dependents snapshot only per[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the Gate, extend SL20, add trigger/hide_removed JSON and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]surfaced/project-empty human rows, add CLI PP tests including PP23, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]measure performance.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Project pull-in in task-status-cycler, with whole-line undo[/bold #D7AFFF]   [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]cycler[dim] · [dim][/dim]after contract[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]cycler: add 089-successor-project.js (surface predicate, #hide strip, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]pull-in planner) and the 137 mixin, relax the gate, integrate in 085, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]store whole-line receipts in 136, add notice copy in 087, emit reason [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]project for still-blocked residents, test the PP vectors, bump, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]deploy on this host.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Render pull-in and project rows in nav's Unblocked card[/bold #D7AFFF]       [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]nav[dim] · [dim][/dim]after contract[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]nav: in 285-unblocked-notice.js add the no-open-tasks chip, the Project [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]empty title, the still-blocked pull-in suffix, the project member label [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and blocked-by-project copy (also for legacy [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]project_dependency/project_schedule reasons), mirror the fallback text, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]test, bump, and deploy on this host.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Install, verify on a vault copy, reach the MacBook, and record[bold black on #87D7FF][/bold #D7AFFF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]rollout[dim] · [dim][/dim]after cli-capture, cycler, nav[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]rollout: